<figure class="flex flex-col gap-4 border-2 border-ink p-4 sm:p-6">
  <p class="font-bold">Three meanings of “pick a random chord”</p>
  <svg
    class="mx-auto w-full max-w-sm"
    viewBox="0 0 300 128"
    role="img"
    aria-labelledby="bertrand-methods-title bertrand-methods-desc"
  >
    <title id="bertrand-methods-title">Three circle and chord diagrams</title>
    <desc id="bertrand-methods-desc">
      All three methods choose chords in a circle. They sample different things, producing
      different chances of exceeding the triangle side.
    </desc>
    {[50, 150, 250].map((x) => (
      <g>
        <circle cx={x} cy="50" r="44" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" />
        <circle
          cx={x}
          cy="50"
          r="22"
          fill="#d7a13d"
          fill-opacity=".3"
          stroke="#d7a13d"
          stroke-dasharray="4 4"
          stroke-width="2"
        />
      </g>
    ))}
    <path
      d="M21.7 16.3 L78.3 83.7 M165 8.6 V91.4 M272 12 L212 72"
      fill="none"
      stroke="#bd4b37"
      stroke-width="3"
    />
    <circle cx="242" cy="42" r="3.5" fill="#bd4b37" />
    <g fill="currentColor" font-size="18" text-anchor="middle">
      <text x="50" y="118">
        1/3
      </text>
      <text x="150" y="118">
        1/2
      </text>
      <text x="250" y="118">
        1/4
      </text>
    </g>
  </svg>
  <div class="overflow-x-auto">
    <table class="w-full text-base">
      <thead>
        <tr class="border-b border-ink">
          <th class="p-2 text-left">What is sampled uniformly?</th>
          <th class="p-2 text-right">Chance of a long chord</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr class="border-b border-ink">
          <td class="p-2">Two points on the circle’s edge</td>
          <td class="p-2 text-right">1/3</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-ink">
          <td class="p-2">The chord’s distance from the centre</td>
          <td class="p-2 text-right">1/2</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="p-2">The chord’s midpoint by area</td>
          <td class="p-2 text-right">1/4</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <figcaption class="text-base leading-normal">
    The dashed inner circle has half the radius. Long chords have midpoints inside it. That
    means half of the possible distances, but only a quarter of the possible midpoint area. The
    pictured chords are examples, not the full random distributions.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
